<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">David Toro</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1898–1977</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> Toro was a Bolivian army officer who served in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chaco-war">Chaco War</a> and became president after a military coup in May 1936. His government proclaimed 'military socialism', created a ministry of labour, founded the state oil company YPFB and in 1937 confiscated the holdings of Standard Oil. He was overthrown in July 1937 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-busch">Germán Busch</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/david-toro.jpg" alt="David Toro" width="320" height="459" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Luigi Domenico Gismondi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:David_Toro._Gismondi,_Luigi_Domenico._c._1936._La_Paz.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
